SessionEnd, Stop, and SubagentStop drive the store's single removeSession contract, which removes records, tombstones, activity entries, and index entries, and SubagentStop's agentId-scoped removal depends on the Codex snapshot adapter recording agent_id on the record — a session's state never outlives its session and a completed subagent's records never mis-attribute a later sibling's writes. The sweep and whole-session removeSession also reap foreign records (v1 leftovers immediately, unreadable files on TTL by mtime) so a v1 upgrade never leaves the store bricked at the storage cap. The store's TTL-sweep, upgrade-reclamation, and removeSession checks and the cleanup/asymmetry harness sections pin that contract.
